<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Guarded. Identity/construction-feature trait — a flared crossguard lets the wielder catch
       and turn aside an incoming blow. Gated on the weapon's
       physical shape via the UMW_Guarded category (longsword/gladius only — see that category's
       file comment), not on an exclusionTags family the way mechanism traits are; "Guard" is instead
       the family token this trait ITSELF seeds for future guard-shape members (riposte, a
       sword-breaker's bind) so at most one guard-family effect ever stacks.
       The effect is a true PARRY, not a stat: MeleeParryExtension gives each incoming melee blow
       that beats both the attacker's hit roll and the wielder's dodge roll a flat chance to be
       caught on the guard and negated, with its own battle-log line (UMW_Combat_Parry), the metal
       deflect ping and a "Parried" mote — resolved by Verb_MeleeAttackDamage_Parry_Patch, which
       mirrors dodge's gates (no parry when surprised, downed or aiming a ranged verb). Deliberately
       NOT an equipped MeleeDodgeChance hediff: that vehicle is bladelink's psychic-bond idiom and
       reads as a pawn condition, where a parry chance IS the hardware working; a flat roll also
       serves conscript and master alike, where a raw dodge offset decays to ~nothing through the
       stat's curve. Sizing lives on the extension class header (0.10 ~ net avoidance +9pp mid-skill,
       against +6pp for the hediff shape — a deliberate touch stronger for melee's risk premium).
       MV +50 offset (added capability, not a scaling/devaluation factor): priced at parity with
       Odyssey's ranged QuickReload — the nearest survivability/combat-tempo utility buff at this
       tier (below AimAssistance's +70 accuracy swing, above CustomGrip's +15 cosmetic-adjacent
       nudge). canGenerateAlone defaults true: a quilloned guard is a complete, nameable identity on its own,
       though UMW_Lightweight backstops generation regardless (every weapon's UMW_Melee membership
       guarantees an alone-able, adjective-bearing trait even if Quilloned doesn't roll first). -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_Quilloned</defName>
    <label>quilloned</label>
    <description>Quillons flare wide from the hilt, letting the wielder catch incoming blows and turn them aside.</description>
    <commonality>1</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Guarded</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Guard</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <statOffsets>
      <MarketValue>50</MarketValue> <!-- cf. QuickReload -->
    </statOffsets>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeParryExtension">
        <parryChance>0.1</parryChance>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>quilloned</li>
      <li>cross-guarded</li>
      <li>warding</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
